# Next.js 16 & Performance Optimization
- Framework: Next.js 16 (Stable, App Router)
- PPR (Partial Prerendering): Actively utilize PPR to combine static shells with dynamic island data.
- Optimized Caching: Adhere to Next.js 16's 'Uncached by default' policy. Use cache: 'force-cache' only when explicitly required.
- Request Memoization: Leverage Next.js internal memoization for data fetching.
- RSC First Strategy: Default to React Server Components. Use 'use client' strictly for leaf-level components requiring interactivity.

# Conventions
- Naming: Use kebab-case for all file names and component names (e.g., job-detail-card.tsx).
- Components: Always use Arrow Functions.
- Logic Separation: Abstract business logic, complex data fetching, and API calls into hooks/ or services/.